    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31412" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nŭmĕrĭus</span></b> , a,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the name of a
				Roman</i> gens. So, Q. Numerius Rufus, <i>a
				tribune of the people</i>, A. U. C. 697, <i>an
				enemy of Cicero</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Sest. 33, 72</span></i>; <i><span class="en">38,
			82</span></i>; <i><span class="en">43, 94</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nŭmĕrĭānus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to a Numerius, Numerian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">raudusculum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 7, 2, 7</span></i>
			.</div>
